<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Consider</h1>
<p>SKILL
</p><p>Class and level:
</p>
<pre> Assassin    - 0
 Barbarian   - 0
 Conjurer    - 0
 Dark Knight - 0
 Druid       - 0
 Fighter     - 0
 Healer      - 3
 Paladin     - 0
 Ranger      - 0
 Sorcerer    - 3
 Thief       - 0
</pre>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>consider &lt;character&gt;
</pre>
<p>Example:
</p>
<pre>consider beast
</pre>
<p>If you are wondering whether an opponent is too strong for you, use this command 
to see if you would have even the slightest chance. Some monsters are simply so 
strong that they may kill you in one hit, and this command will help you know.
</p><p>Be aware that it doesn't consider whether nearby monsters will help the one you 
attack, or whether it has special attacks like a breath weapon or spells: these 
are the risks you must run. It assumes you have full hit points, and it doesn't 
count others who may help you. The better your consider skill, the more accurate 
your judgement.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
